y of the actions above and follow-ups. The follow-ups are to find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health check failures, look into the orchestrator partial failure, and confirm a fix before redeploying v2.3.1.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LpsN8c9w4tnAszCULp6h7B", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Hw4KDWC6uWBXQr4oPLGPSZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy production release, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Rolling back to v2.3.0, which has already run healthy in production, so it doesn't need change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LbYnqEZRLrFmTsKs1ARan6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state of each region before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018nsQRi9W13geL8Co3KxyTm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018nM9hMgVgq5uiZHVP1Hr2n", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "",